\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri-494\widctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin-494\lin0\itap0 {\f1 The picture/image view utility, included in the 4nec2 package, is a helper program for the 4nec2 
and ItsHF/HFwin32 programs. It is used to view one or more ItsHF area-coverage or point-to-point output plot-files. It is most important quality is the ability to visualize and compare differences between two or more plot-files.
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri-494\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin-494\lin0\itap0 {\f1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid0\langnp1033 
\par There are three possibilities to Open and view pictures/plot-files:
\par 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\cgrid0 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 1)\tab}}\pard \qj \fi-360\li360\ri-494\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx360\faauto\ls31\adjustright\rin-494\lin360\itap0 {\f1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid0\langnp1033 Open and load *.bmp bitmap file(s)

\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri-494\nowidctlpar\faauto\adjustright\rin-494\lin0\itap0 {\f1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid0\langnp1033 2)\tab Open, run ItsHF plot-program and copy/paste *.ig1, *.rg1 or  *.vg1 plot-file(s)
\par 3)\tab Paste any given clipboard picture.
\par 
\par When using }{\f1\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid0\langnp1033 method 1)}{\f1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid0\langnp1033  you enter *.bmp in the \lquote Open file\rquote 
 dialog window as the file-type to open. Next a list of available bitmp files is displayed and you select the required *.bmp bitmap file which is directly loaded and displayed on the screen. 
\par 
\par When the last two characters of the selected filename are numeric, the program checks if there are more files with the same (base) name and an increasing last two ch
aracter numeric suffix. If so, the available number of similar files is displayed, and you are asked how many files to load. All these files are loaded as one sequence.
\par 
\par When using }{\f1\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid0\langnp1033 method 2)}{\f1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid0\langnp1033  you select enter *.ig1 (icepac), *.rg1 (rec533) or *.vg1 (voacap) as the filetype to open in the \lquote Open File\rquote 
 dialog window. All available files of that type are listed and you select the required plot-file you want to see on the screen.
\par 
\par When a certain plot-file is selected, first, the ItsHF plotting program is started 
to load and display the plot-file data. Depending on the view.exe program-settings, this image is then automatically copied and pasted into the Viewer program, or you may manually copy the image by using then Alt-T (copy to clipboard) followed by the Alt-
X (exit program). Use \lquote File->Autmatic copy/paste\rquote  to enable or disable automatic copying
\par When the selected file contains a numeric last two-character suffix, and two or more similar files are available, you are asked for the number of files to load. All these files are then loaded, plotted and copied as one sequence.
\par 
\par When using }{\f1\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid0\langnp1033 method 3)}{\f1\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid0\langnp1033 
 you are able to paste the current content of the clipboard in the picture-viewer program. This could be used to include pictures from other sources. You can copy any pictur
e to the clipboard by selecting the appropriate window and use the Ctrl together with the Print Screen key.
\par 
\par If two or more pictures are loaded, with the Up- and Down-arrow key\rquote s it is possible to switch very quickly between the different pictures. So differences are easily noticed.
\par 
\par When the program is closed and *.ig1, *.rg1, *.vg1 or clipboard pictures are loaded, you are asked if the loaded pictures should be saved as *.bmp bitmap images, so it is easy to reload them the n
ext time. If this is confirmed, the program checks if a range of pictures with numeric suffixes is available. If so, you are asked for the number of pictures to save. All these pictures are saved as one sequence.
\par 
\par 
